---
name: changelog-entry
description: Write the changelog entry of one change from its change.json. Use when the user asks for the changelog line of a change.
---
# changelog-entry

Read `change.json` in the working directory.
Apply the rules of `references/format.md` to write one changelog entry.
Write the entry to `entry.md`.
Then return one JSON object as the answer, and nothing else: `{"entry": "<the entry line>"}`.

## Input

`change.json` holds one JSON object with these keys:

- `ticket`: an id such as `ABC-123`, or `null`.
- `type`: `feat`, `fix`, `perf`, `docs`, or `refactor`.
- `scope`: one lowercase word, or `null`.
- `summary`: one line of text.
- `breaking`: `true` or `false`.

## Helper

`scripts/change-check.pyz` checks that `change.json` holds these keys with valid values:

```sh
python3 .agents/skills/changelog-entry/scripts/change-check.pyz change.json
```

It prints `{"ok": true}`, or an error with exit code 3.

No helper writes the entry yet. Apply the rules of `references/format.md` by hand to every change.
